## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end security of hybrid AI platforms, spanning software supply chain and model governance, with practical incident response capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- Secure software supply chain and model governance
- SBOMs, image/model signing, and cryptographic attestations
- Provenance verification and reproducible builds
- Policy-as-Code enforcement with OPA Gatekeeper
- Runtime attestation in Kubernetes environments
- Data provenance tracking for training datasets
- Incident response playbooks and success metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: sign an image with cosign
const { execSync } = require('child_process');

function signContainerImage(imageUrl) {
  // Generate SBOM
  execSync(`syft ${imageUrl} -o cyclonedx-json > sbom.json`);

  // Sign the image
  execSync(`cosign sign --key cosign.key ${imageUrl}`);

  // Attach SBOM as attestation
  execSync(`cosign attest --predicate sbom.json --type cyclonedx ${imageUrl}`);

  console.log(`Successfully signed ${imageUrl}`);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests ability to design practical, compliant data access controls across serverless and containerized services, with ABAC, key management, RBAC, policy-as-code, and IR planning.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC attributes and enforcement points
- MongoDB Atlas RBAC & Client-Side Encryption
- AWS KMS key management and rotation
- Policy-as-code (OPA) integration and CI gates
- Incident response timing and evidence collection

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-authorization check example
function hasAccess(attrs, request) {
  const {service, tenant, data_class, operation, region} = attrs;
  const r = request;
  return r.service === service && r.tenant === tenant && r.data_class === data_class && r.operation === operation && r.region === region;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test ABAC policies in CI/CD and simulate breaches?
- How would you audit data access for forensics and regulatory reporting?

